      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if this is the exact right time to do this. At least one of the policies (`enforce_pd_chipset_resume_policy_1`) will only do the expected PRS if the port is in a sink state. But I don\u0027t think the power management task is in a position to know that until the `CMD_PDC_GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS` returns.\n\nI\u0027m not sure exactly what the right time would be, but I think you could avoid this particular issue by having a policy flag that would trigger a call to `pdc_handle_late_sysjump`. That would mean that these changes wouldn\u0027t be applied until the task was in steady state. As a perhaps unwanted side effect, the port would do all of the normal activities for, say, Attached.SRC, before deciding that it should really be in Attached.SNK.\n\nAnother option would be to try to define the suspend/resume/shutdown policies in terms of role-policy flags that could be applied unconditionally, and each role-state would apply the flags as the situation warranted. This would result in the same state flow as I described above, and it would require some refactoring. However, it might make the power-state policies more robust generally, and it would avoid having a catch-all policy flag that just sets other policy flags.",
      "revId": "fe919ec3177fede243ecf3bd05a50720dc31c58e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
